<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Protestant Reformation</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Reformation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Protestant Reformation was the religious movement of the sixteenth century, begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> in 1517, that broke with the Roman Catholic Church and created Protestant churches. It began in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, where princes' adoption of the new faiths led to religious wars. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-augsburg">Peace of Augsburg</a> in 1555 left the empire divided along confessional lines.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation.jpg" alt="Protestant Reformation" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shizhao; derivative work by 6birc · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:95Thesen_facsimile_colour.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
